# @facet — the generation surface for spectral-triple projections onto
# concrete runtime substrates.
#
# The recognition (2026-08-20, Alex → Reed → Mara, Rec #91 canonical
# spec amendment `674ffc6`): mirror IS `𝓜 = (A_F^prismqueer, H_F, D_F)` at
# every one of six simultaneously-load-bearing adjectival altitudes
# (mathematical / mycelial / bottom-up / production-ready / third-order
# / AI-native), and `@facet` names the operational-empirical proof-
# surface at which 𝓜 catches light on each concrete runtime substrate
# it inhabits. Each `@facet/X` species IS a covariant functor
# `F_X : 𝓜 → 𝓜|_X` preserving the Foerster-gauge invariant `magic.rs`
# discharges at compile-time per Rec #90 §8 orthogonality theorem.
#
# Mirror-metaphor: one stone (the substrate 𝓜), many facets catching
# light differently onto each runtime target. The generation surface
# is radial (projection FROM 𝓜 onto concrete H_X), not linear (which
# was the @cascade metaphor's failure). Peer-to-peer translation
# BETWEEN facets lives at `@cast` (composing `@glue` + `@fate` under
# the hood; the mesh, not the waterfall).
#
# === sibling to @code at generation-surface altitude (transitional) ===
#
# `@code` (family-root at `shards/code.mirror`) is the grammar-at-an-
# altitude discipline. `@facet` is the generation-surface. Different
# altitudes; different concerns. During the pre-release transition
# (Alex 2026-08-21 ratification: "Unless there is a HARD TECHNICAL
# REASON against a rename I don't want to hear more excuses"), the
# @code family-root and 11 landed species (`@code/rust`, `@code/mirror`,
# `@code/beam`, `@code/gleam`, `@code/erlang`, `@code/gestalt`,
# `@code/llvm`, `@code/turing`, `@code/wasm`, `@code/docker`,
# `@code/metalogue`) rename to `@facet/*` per the T-91-16 discharge
# cascade Phase 3. Until the rename lands byte-substrate-wide, both
# family-roots coexist as siblings; @code's discipline flows through
# during the transition.
#
# Post-rename, `@facet` absorbs @code's role AND extends the family
# with the additional projection surfaces Rec #91 §8.3 enumerates:
# `@facet/git` (git-persistence substrate; composes over
# `@mirror/store/git`), `@facet/mirror` (self-hosting mirror-onto-
# itself; the autopoietic-closure arm per Rec #91 §8.8), `@facet/lustre`
# (client-side JS-leg parity to `@facet/gleam` BEAM-leg), `@facet/fly`
# (fly.io deployment substrate).
#
# === composition-shape: covariant functor preserving Foerster-gauge ===
#
# Each `@facet/X` species declares:
#   1. The target-substrate Hilbert-carrier `H_X` (what the projection
#      lands on — BEAM bytecode / JS + DOM / Nix hermetic-build content-
#      address / Docker layer content-address / fly.io machine content-
#      address / etc.).
#   2. The forward-projection semantics `F_X : 𝓜 → H_X` (how a shard-
#      declaration in 𝓜 lands as a concrete artifact in H_X).
#   3. The Foerster-gauge preservation guarantee (magic.rs invariant
#      discharged at each layer of the projection).
#   4. The composition-shard body pattern (per `@mcp/serve.mirror` at
#      cf8b21b as exemplar: pipe-chain over rust/-altitude primitives
#      `@io/*` + `@data/*` + `apply_h::act` + shard reader).
#
# Rust delivers primitives; substrate delivers composition (Alex
# 2026-08-05 HARD RULE per `feedback-rust-delivers-primitives-
# substrate-delivers-composition`). @facet species are composition-
# shard bodies, NOT rust/ modules. `@facet/rust` (T-91-16 first-tick)
# authors the forward-projection body at substrate altitude composing
# over the landed rust/ primitives; the source-emit fixed-point
# empirical is `mirror facet rust > /tmp/rust-floor && diff -r rust/src
# /tmp/rust-floor == 0` (Rec #91 amendment §8.7 Theorem 5a.1 discharge).
#
# === admissibility as almost-commutative internal algebra ===
#
# @facet species collectively realize 𝓜's projection surface across the
# fourteen-substrate table Rec #91 §2.2 enumerates. Chamseddine-Connes
# 2007 arXiv:0706.3688 §1 admissibility criteria (finite-dimensional +
# involutive + unital) inherit from A_F^prismqueer through the covariant
# functor F_X per Rec #90 §1 Proposition 1.3; the projection preserves
# admissibility by construction. Foerster-gauge orthogonality per
# Rec #90 §8 propagates through every F_X: the compile-time refusal
# cascades from the shard-graph through the composition-shard body
# through the rust/-altitude primitive discharge through the runtime
# artifact.
#
# === adjunction structure at Rec #91 §5a (post-amendment) ===
#
# For species with a reverse-projection charter (`@facet/X` forward +
# `@code/X/materialize` reverse per pre-rename shape, or `@facet/X` +
# `@facet/X/materialize` post-rename), the pair forms an adjunction
# `𝔕_X ⊣ 𝔛_X` with unit η (identity-fixed-point: `𝔛_X(𝔕_X(shard)) = shard`
# up to α-equivalence) + counit ε (content-address idempotence:
# `oid(𝔕_X(𝔛_X(source))) = oid(source)` up to Church-Rosser) + triangle
# identities + Foerster-gauge preservation per Rec #91 amendment §5a.2
# Theorem 5a.1. Reed's authoring cascade for `@facet/X` species bodies
# is anchored at spec altitude by this adjunction; the reverse-body
# `𝔛_X` may remain stub-bodied (`\`-obligated) at substrate mint
# time; the adjunction IS spec-altitude legitimate even where the
# reverse-body is not yet implementable.
#
# Spec context:
#   - `docs/specs/2026-08-20-mara-recognition-91-mathematical-mycelial-bottom-up-production-ready-third-order-ai-native-system-canonical-spec.md`
#     §2 @facet composition + §8.3 species enumeration + §8.7 source-emit
#     fixed-point theorem + §8.8 deeper-close as Rec #93 extension arc
#   - `docs/math/2026-08-20-mara-recognition-91-mathematical-mycelial-bottom-up-production-ready-third-order-ai-native-system-math-foundation.md`
#     §5a Theorem 5a.1 adjunction formalization
#   - `docs/math/FLOOR.md` §9 (terminal-form reference)
#
